   233	These defaults can be replaced with entries in the configured MapStruct properties resource:
   234	
   235	[source, properties]
   236	----
   237	mapstruct.collectionImplementation.java.util.List=com.example.MyList
   238	mapstruct.collectionImplementation.java.util.Map=com.example.MyMap
   239	----
   240	
   241	The default resource is `mapstruct.properties` at the root of the mapping compilation classpath.
   242	The `mapstruct.configurationFile` annotation processor option selects a different resource by relative path on the same classpath.
   243	MapStruct does not resolve either resource from the annotation processor's own classloader.
   244	
   245	The configured type can be part of the current compilation or generated in a later annotation processing round.
   246	It must be a publicly accessible concrete class assignable to the configured interface, preserve the interface's unbounded type parameters, and provide a public no-argument constructor that declares no checked exceptions.
   247	If it also provides a usable public `int` constructor, MapStruct passes the source size as the initial capacity.
   248	An applicable object factory continues to take precedence over the configured implementation.
   249	
   250	Unknown properties, unsupported interfaces, empty values, conflicting duplicate entries, and invalid or unresolved implementation types cause compilation to fail.
   251	Equal duplicate entries are permitted.
   252	The configured implementation applies whenever MapStruct constructs that exact supported interface result, including bean properties and stream mappings.
